 "caveats": [
  "Selection: Singlet's setting for each dataset was chosen among 120 fixed settings of one caller family on the other three datasets (bench/adt/hto_lodo.py; criterion fixed in advance: mean of F minus genetic doublets called singlets), so no Singlet value is tuned on its own dataset. The paper's 'optimised' hashedDrops was tuned by its authors on these same datasets.",
  "Only these four datasets have an independent per-cell truth together with hashtag counts, so selection saw three datasets at a time. pbmc-ch, cline-ch and mkidney-ch (Xi & Li) label doublets from the hashtags themselves and are not independent truth for hashtag calls.",
  "F-score and genetic doublets called singlets trade off: the best competitor on one is rarely the best on the other (for example hashedDrops-optimised has the best F-score and calls 41-68% of genetic doublets singlets in BAL2, BAL3 and the cell lines). The Singlet setting favours few doublet calls.",
  "demuxEM is not compared: it needs RNA counts of empty droplets, which this benchmark does not include.",
  "Competitors from the paper's published calls were run by its authors with their versions and settings."
 ]
}